x. This is a crucial step for flashing firmware. Different keyboards have d=
ifferent methods, but I should cover the common ones for Sofle keyboards.</=
p></div></div></div></div></div></div></div><div><div class=3D"grid-cols-1 =
grid gap-2.5 [&amp;_&gt;_*]:min-w-0"><h2 class=3D"text-xl font-bold text-te=
xt-100 mt-1 -mb-0.5">Ways to Enter Bootloader Mode on Sofle Choc:</h2>
<h3 class=3D"text-lg font-bold text-text-100 mt-1 -mb-1.5">1. <strong>Physi=
cal Reset Button</strong> (Most Common)</h3>
<ul class=3D"[&amp;:not(:last-child)_ul]:pb-1 [&amp;:not(:last-child)_ol]:p=
b-1 list-disc space-y-1.5 pl-7">
<li class=3D"whitespace-normal break-words"><strong>Look on the PCB</strong=
> (bottom of keyboard) for a small button labeled "RESET" or "RST"</li>
<li class=3D"whitespace-normal break-words">Press it once quickly</li>
<li class=3D"whitespace-normal break-words">The keyboard will enter bootloa=
der mode for ~8 seconds</li>
<li class=3D"whitespace-normal break-words">QMK Toolbox will show "*** DFU =
device connected"</li>
</ul>
<h3 class=3D"text-lg font-bold text-text-100 mt-1 -mb-1.5">2. <strong>Reset=
 Pins/Pads</strong> (If no button)</h3>
<ul class=3D"[&amp;:not(:last-child)_ul]:pb-1 [&amp;:not(:last-child)_ol]:p=
b-1 list-disc space-y-1.5 pl-7">
<li class=3D"whitespace-normal break-words">Look for two pads labeled "RESE=
T" or "RST" and "GND"</li>
<li class=3D"whitespace-normal break-words">Use metal tweezers or paperclip=
 to short them briefly</li>
<li class=3D"whitespace-normal break-words">Common locations: near the micr=
ocontroller or TRRS jack</li>
</ul>
<h3 class=3D"text-lg font-bold text-text-100 mt-1 -mb-1.5">3. <strong>Bootm=
agic</strong> (Hold key while plugging in)</h3>
<ul class=3D"[&amp;:not(:last-child)_ul]:pb-1 [&amp;:not(:last-child)_ol]:p=
b-1 list-disc space-y-1.5 pl-7">
<li class=3D"whitespace-normal break-words">Unplug keyboard</li>
<li class=3D"whitespace-normal break-words">Hold <strong>top-left key</stro=
ng> (usually Escape position)</li>
<li class=3D"whitespace-normal break-words">While holding, plug in USB cabl=
e</li>
<li class=3D"whitespace-normal break-words">Keep holding for 2-3 seconds</l=
i>
</ul>
<h3 class=3D"text-lg font-bold text-text-100 mt-1 -mb-1.5">4. <strong>Reset=
 Keycode</strong> (If already programmed)</h3>
<ul class=3D"[&amp;:not(:last-child)_ul]:pb-1 [&amp;:not(:last-child)_ol]:p=
b-1 list-disc space-y-1.5 pl-7">
<li class=3D"whitespace-normal break-words">If the current firmware has a R=
ESET key mapped:
<ul class=3D"[&amp;:not(:last-child)_ul]:pb-1 [&amp;:not(:last-child)_ol]:p=
b-1 list-disc space-y-1.5 pl-7">
<li class=3D"whitespace-normal break-words">Usually on a layer (like Fn + B=
ackspace)</li>
<li class=3D"whitespace-normal break-words">Check the default Sofle layout =
for the reset key location</li>
</ul>
</li>
</ul>
